meta {
  name: Update Notification Preferences
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}/notification-preferences
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "optOutChannels": ["SMS"],
    "optOutFeatures": {
      "lab_order_report_published_inform_patient": ["WHATSAPP"]
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Replace a patient's notification opt-out preferences (a full write). Unknown
  feature keys and non-deliverable channels are sanitised out server-side; an
  empty result clears the field (opted into everything). Scoped to the caller's
  tenant.

  Read by `NotificationEnablementService` to gate AUTOMATIC notifications: a
  channel here is dropped for that patient (globally via `optOutChannels`, or for
  the specific feature via `optOutFeatures`). Returns the normalised preferences.

  ## Fields (all optional)
  - `optOutChannels[]`: `EMAIL` | `SMS` | `WHATSAPP` (opt out for all features).
  - `optOutFeatures`: `{ [FEATURE_TYPES key]: MessagingChannel[] }` (per-feature).
}
